# Parity fixture matrix (refactor Slice 0)

Shared inputs for the browser↔CLI comparison required by
`specs/007-renderer-export/contracts/parity.md`. Both sides read this file; a
change here changes the comparison set on both sides in the same commit.

Fields per case: `id`, `lat`, `lon`, `place`, `when_utc` (ISO-8601, UTC), `tz`,
`options`, `size_px`.

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "tolerance": {
    "channel_mean_abs": 25,
    "channel_max_excluding_edges": 255,
    "notes": "Per-channel 0-255 over RGB, alpha ignored. MEASURED, not chosen: the browser↔CLI gap is meanAbs 10.6-19.5 across this matrix, so 25 is the pass bar with headroom, and maxAbs is not meaningful as a gate (255 at star/label edges). The residual is antialiasing (matplotlib LANCZOS vs Chromium) plus the glow falloff (scatter alpha vs radial gradient) — differences two rasterisers cannot be asked to make identical. STRUCTURE is the real contract and is checked separately: star core area 3208 vs 3203 px and caption strings are identical on nyc-newyear-circle; star/segment/label COUNTS do differ today (browser merges neighbouring cores: 77 blobs vs 130) and the poster default must not flip until that is explained or fixed."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "nyc-newyear-circle",
      "lat": 40.758,
      "lon": -73.9855,
      "place": "Times Square",
      "when_utc": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "tz": "America/New_York",
      "options": {"magnitude_limit": 4.5, "shape": "circle", "title": "New Year"},
      "size_px": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "sydney-xmas-square",
      "lat": -33.8688,
      "lon": 151.2093,
      "place": "Sydney",
      "when_utc": "2025-12-25T11:00:00Z",
      "tz": "Australia/Sydney",
      "options": {"magnitude_limit": 5.0, "shape": "square", "glow": false},
      "size_px": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "reykjavik-fisheye",
      "lat": 64.1466,
      "lon": -21.9426,
      "place": "Reykjavik",
      "when_utc": "2025-12-21T23:00:00Z",
      "tz": "Atlantic/Reykjavik",
      "options": {
        "projection": "fisheye",
        "fisheye_strength": 1.4,
        "magnitude_limit": 6.0,
        "constellation_labels": false,
        "title": "Longest night"
      },
      "size_px": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "cairo-perseids-mins-sep",
      "lat": 29.9792,
      "lon": 31.1342,
      "place": null,
      "when_utc": "2025-08-12T20:30:00Z",
      "tz": "Africa/Cairo",
      "options": {"min_separation": 0.02, "magnitude_limit": 5.8, "shape": "circle"},
      "size_px": 320
    },
    {
      "id": "nagahama-heritage",
      "lat": 35.3786,
      "lon": 136.2664,
      "place": "Nagahama",
      "when_utc": "1998-11-17T02:17:00Z",
      "tz": "Asia/Tokyo",
      "options": {"magnitude_limit": 3.5, "glow_intensity": 2.0},
      "size_px": 320
    }
  ]
}
```

Rendering the cases needs the ephemeris + catalog caches; the harness that
consumes it is added in refactor Slice 3, when the browser renderer exists.
The CLI side is `scripts/render_parity_fixtures.py`.
